 "text": "Hey there, how are you? Lisbon is a great city to explore on foot, with lots of little cafes and boutiques. Have you explored the Belem Tower and Jerónimo's Convent? Then head to the Bairro Alto, the old district with the pretty streets. Of course. You can paint over it with a thin base coat, or you can cut it out and replace it. You can leave them if they're healthy. Go up to the maintenance window and ask for a fresh cut branch. Stick it in through the door you use most. No worries. Go back up and stick it in, then forget about it for few weeks.",
